    44	**<span class="mark">Am I eligible for weight loss surgery in
    45	Perth?</span>**
    46	
    47	<span class="mark">If you have spent years trying to lose weight and
    48	keep finding yourself back where you started, you are not alone, and it
    49	is not a failure of willpower. Obesity is a medical condition and, like
    50	any medical condition, it responds better to proper treatment than to
    51	trying harder. This page walks you through who is eligible for weight
    52	loss surgery in Perth, what your BMI and health history mean in
    53	practice, and what to expect when you meet us.</span>
    54	
    55	**<span class="mark">Eligibility is about more than a single
    56	number</span>**
    57	
    58	<span class="mark">Most people start by asking whether their BMI is high
    59	enough. It is a fair question, and BMI does form part of the picture.
    60	But eligibility for weight loss surgery is not decided by a single
    61	number. When you meet your Obesity Surgery WA surgeon, they will review
    62	your weight, your whole health history, what you have already tried, and
    63	what you want your life to look like in five or ten years.</span>
    64	
    65	<span class="mark">Technically, body mass index (BMI) is your weight in
    66	kilograms divided by your height in metres squared. As a guide for
    67	Australians: a BMI of ~27 to 29 sits in the overweight range, ~30 to 34
    68	is class 1 obesity, ~35 to 39 is class 2 obesity, and ~40 and above is
    69	class 3, sometimes called severe obesity. Your BMI influences which
    70	options are likely to suit you, but it does not tell the whole story on
    71	its own.</span>
    72	
    73	<span class="mark">Two people can have the same BMI and receive very
    74	different recommendations. Someone at BMI 32 with type 2 diabetes and
    75	sleep apnoea, for example, may be a strong surgical candidate, while
    76	someone at the same BMI with no related health conditions might be
    77	better placed starting with a medical or dietitian-led program.</span>
    78	
    79	| <span class="mark">You do not need to know your BMI before getting in touch; our team can help you work it out, and your surgeon will measure and confirm it at your consultation.</span> |
    80	|----|
    81	
    82	### **<span class="mark">Is weight loss surgery suitable for you? </span>**
    83	
    84	| <span class="mark">As a general guide, surgical assessment is typically available for those with a BMI of ~35, and almost always from 40 and higher. Someone with a BMI of 30 to 34 may qualify where weight-related health conditions such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, or sleep apnoea are present and there have been previous attempts at weight loss through diet, exercise, or non-surgical means without lasting success. Please note that these are general clinical indicators only; your surgeon will make a clinical assessment and discuss your options with you when you meet.</span> |
