   179	
   180	### **<span class="mark">What to understand before you decide Alt An honest word on what surgery involves</span>**
   181	
   182	Being eligible for weight loss surgery does not automatically make it
   183	the right choice for you. Part of Obesity Surgery WA’s assessment
   184	process is making sure you understand the commitment and the risks
   185	involved so that whatever you decide, you decide with a clear picture of
   186	what’s involved.
   187	
   188	- <span class="mark">All surgery carries risk including bleeding,
   189	  infection, blood clots, and adverse reactions to anaesthetic.</span>
   190	
   191	- <span class="mark">Bariatric procedures require lifelong changes to
   192	  how you eat and ongoing follow-up with your care team.</span>
   193	
   194	- <span class="mark">Some procedures require long-term vitamin and
   195	  mineral supplementation, particularly those that affect nutrient
   196	  absorption such as the gastric bypass.</span>
   197	
   198	- <span class="mark">Results depend on adherence to dietary and
   199	  lifestyle guidance after surgery, and outcomes vary between
   200	  individuals.</span>
   201	
   202	- <span class="mark">Surgery is a powerful tool, but it works best when
   203	  supported by the habits and care built around it — it is not a
   204	  standalone cure.</span>
   205	
   206	### **<span class="mark">Weight loss surgery cost </span>**
   207	
   208	<span class="mark">The cost of weight loss surgery in Perth varies
   209	depending on the procedure, your level of private health cover, your
   210	hospital excess, and anaesthetist fees. For patients with appropriate
   211	private health insurance (typically a gold-tier or equivalent policy) a
   212	significant portion of the overall cost is covered, and Medicare rebates
   213	apply when eligibility criteria are met. For those without private
   214	health cover, or where out-of-pocket costs are a concern, financing
   215	options such as Zip and TLC are available, and accessing your
   216	superannuation for weight loss surgery may be possible in certain
   217	circumstances. Before any commitment is made, our team provides a clear,
   218	itemised breakdown of what applies to your situation. Before any
   219	commitment is made, our team provides a clear, itemised breakdown of
   220	every cost that applies to your situation so there are no
   221	surprises.</span>
