   224	
   225	<span class="mark">Not sure where to start? We’re here to help.  
   226	Alt  
   227	You don’t need a plan yet. You just need a conversation.</span>
   228	
   229	### <span class="mark">FAQs (7 questions)</span>
   230	
   231	<span class="mark">The page must answer each of the following:</span>
   232	
   233	<span class="mark">**1. My BMI is around 30; am I too low for weight
   234	loss surgery?  **
   235	Not necessarily. A BMI of 30-34 may qualify for a surgical pathway when
   236	weight-related health conditions such as type 2 diabetes, high blood
   237	pressure, or sleep apnoea are present. If surgery is not the right
   238	starting point, our medical team can offer meaningful support through
   239	medication and dietitian-led care. The only way to know where you stand
   240	is a proper assessment.</span>
   241	
   242	<span class="mark">**2. I have tried every diet and they all failed.
   243	Does that count against me?  **
   244	Not at all. On the contrary, a history of attempts at non-surgical
   245	weight loss is part of what helps confirm that a more intensive pathway
   246	is likely appropriate. It demonstrates that you have tried, not that you
   247	have failed. Obesity is a medical condition and difficulty losing weight
   248	through diet alone is a clinical reality, not a personal
   249	shortcoming.</span>
   250	
   251	<span class="mark">**3. Will a mental health history stop me from being
   252	eligible?  **
   253	No. Psychological wellbeing is part of the assessment process, but a
   254	mental health history is not a reason to be turned away. A psychological
   255	review is there to set you up for the best possible outcome and make
   256	sure the timing and support are right for you.</span>
   257	
   258	<span class="mark">**4. Do I need a GP referral, or can I refer
   259	myself?  **
   260	You can contact us directly; a GP referral is not required to get
   261	started. That said, a referral is worth having as it allows Medicare
   262	rebates to apply to your specialist consultation fee, reducing your
   263	out-of-pocket cost for the appointment. If you don't have one yet, our
   264	team can advise you on next steps when you get in touch.</span>
   265	
