   267	appointment?  **
   268	Your initial consultation runs for 30-60 minutes and is a relaxed,
   269	honest conversation about your weight history, health, and goals. Your
   270	surgeon explains which options are likely to suit you, walks through the
   271	relevant procedures, and discusses costs openly. You are welcome to ask
   272	as many questions as you like; there is zero obligation to proceed, and
   273	no pressure to decide anything on the day.</span>
   274	
   275	<span class="mark">**6. How long does it take to go from first
   276	consultation to surgery?  **
   277	It varies depending on your individual circumstances, the procedure
   278	involved, and how quickly the assessment and preparation stage
   279	progresses. For some patients it is a matter of weeks; for others it
   280	takes longer, particularly if additional tests or team reviews are
   281	needed. Your surgeon will give you a realistic timeframe at your
   282	consultation based on your specific situation.</span>
   283	
   284	<span class="mark">**7. What if I find out surgery is not right for
   285	me?  **
   286	You will not leave without options. If surgery is not the right fit —
   287	due to timing, preference, or for clinical reasons — we can discuss
   288	medical weight management pathways including GLP-1 medications and
   289	dietitian-led programs. Some patients start there and revisit surgery
   290	later; others find it is sufficient on its own. The goal is the right
   291	outcome for you, whatever form that takes.</span>

