   237	pressure, or sleep apnoea are present. If surgery is not the right
   238	starting point, our medical team can offer meaningful support through
   239	medication and dietitian-led care. The only way to know where you stand
   240	is a proper assessment.</span>
   241	
   242	<span class="mark">**2. I have tried every diet and they all failed.
   243	Does that count against me?  **
   244	Not at all. On the contrary, a history of attempts at non-surgical
   245	weight loss is part of what helps confirm that a more intensive pathway
   246	is likely appropriate. It demonstrates that you have tried, not that you
   247	have failed. Obesity is a medical condition and difficulty losing weight
   248	through diet alone is a clinical reality, not a personal
   249	shortcoming.</span>
   250	
   251	<span class="mark">**3. Will a mental health history stop me from being
   252	eligible?  **
   253	No. Psychological wellbeing is part of the assessment process, but a
   254	mental health history is not a reason to be turned away. A psychological
   255	review is there to set you up for the best possible outcome and make
   256	sure the timing and support are right for you.</span>
   257	
   258	<span class="mark">**4. Do I need a GP referral, or can I refer
   259	myself?  **
   260	You can contact us directly; a GP referral is not required to get
   261	started. That said, a referral is worth having as it allows Medicare
   262	rebates to apply to your specialist consultation fee, reducing your
   263	out-of-pocket cost for the appointment. If you don't have one yet, our
   264	team can advise you on next steps when you get in touch.</span>
   265	
   266	<span class="mark">**5. What actually happens at the first
   267	appointment?  **
   268	Your initial consultation runs for 30-60 minutes and is a relaxed,
   269	honest conversation about your weight history, health, and goals. Your
   270	surgeon explains which options are likely to suit you, walks through the
   271	relevant procedures, and discusses costs openly. You are welcome to ask
   272	as many questions as you like; there is zero obligation to proceed, and
   273	no pressure to decide anything on the day.</span>
   274	
   275	<span class="mark">**6. How long does it take to go from first
   276	consultation to surgery?  **
   277	It varies depending on your individual circumstances, the procedure
   278	involved, and how quickly the assessment and preparation stage
   279	progresses. For some patients it is a matter of weeks; for others it
   280	takes longer, particularly if additional tests or team reviews are
   281	needed. Your surgeon will give you a realistic timeframe at your
   282	consultation based on your specific situation.</span>
   283	
   284	<span class="mark">**7. What if I find out surgery is not right for
   285	me?  **
   286	You will not leave without options. If surgery is not the right fit —
   287	due to timing, preference, or for clinical reasons — we can discuss
   288	medical weight management pathways including GLP-1 medications and
   289	dietitian-led programs. Some patients start there and revisit surgery
   290	later; others find it is sufficient on its own. The goal is the right
   291	outcome for you, whatever form that takes.</span>

