+3. **CTA label and standalone alternate**
+
+> Draft L223-L227: ### Conversion CTA headline
+> Not sure where to start? We’re here to help.  
+> Alt  
+> You don’t need a plan yet. You just need a conversation.
+
+> ### Find out where you stand
+> The hardest part is often making the first call. [Book a consultation](/book-consultation) to discuss your eligibility and options.
+
+4. **Editorial FAQ instruction**
+
+> Draft L229-L231: ### FAQs (7 questions)
+> The page must answer each of the following:
+
+> ### FAQs
+
+Delete the sentence “The page must answer each of the following:” and publish only the patient-facing questions and answers. No “Option A” artifact appears in the draft.
+
+### G5 — brief corrections applied
+
+The brief now:
+
+- Replaces “BMI 35+ — Usually eligible” with individual assessment wording and states the MBS rule as BMI 40+, or BMI 35+ with a major obesity-related comorbidity; BMI below 35 does not meet the MBS threshold for these items.
+- Removes the brief’s “may qualify”, “with or without other health conditions”, “almost everyone eligible” and “most effective long-term option” directions.
