+### G5 — brief corrections applied
+
+The brief now:
+
+- Replaces “BMI 35+ — Usually eligible” with individual assessment wording and states the MBS rule as BMI 40+, or BMI 35+ with a major obesity-related comorbidity; BMI below 35 does not meet the MBS threshold for these items.
+- Removes the brief’s “may qualify”, “with or without other health conditions”, “almost everyone eligible” and “most effective long-term option” directions.
+- Replaces “surgery is safe” with an assessment of appropriateness, risks and preparation.
+- Replaces “never a reason to be turned away” with measured mental-health and aftercare wording.
+- Changes the cost direction to consultation-based estimates and conditional Medicare/private-health wording, with no dollar figures or coverage promises.
+- Adds the pending TGA/legal policy note: prefer neutral non-surgical medical weight-management wording; if active-ingredient/class wording is retained after review, use semaglutide, liraglutide or GLP-1 only and never brand names.
