+> Draft L251-L256: **3. Will a mental health history stop me from being eligible?  **
+> No. Psychological wellbeing is part of the assessment process, but a mental health history is not a reason to be turned away. A psychological review is there to set you up for the best possible outcome and make sure the timing and support are right for you.
+
+> **3. Will a mental health history stop me from being eligible?** A mental health history does not automatically rule out surgery. Psychological wellbeing is part of the assessment, and active or unstable concerns, an untreated eating disorder, substance misuse or difficulty following aftercare may affect timing or suitability. Your surgeon will discuss what support or further review may be needed.
+
+Why it matters: The FAQ is a second occurrence after the eligibility bullet. It must not promise that a mental-health history will never affect suitability or that review will produce a particular outcome.
