+#### Paste-ready FAQ replacement
+
+Replace Draft L284-L291 with:
+
+> **7. What if I find out surgery is not right for me?** Some people are not suitable for surgery straight away, or may not be suitable at all. Reasons can include a medical condition that makes anaesthetic or surgery too risky, pregnancy, active substance misuse, an untreated eating disorder or difficulty safely following the required aftercare. Your surgeon will explain the assessment and discuss non-surgical options where appropriate.
+>
+> **8. How much does weight loss surgery cost in Perth?** There is no single Perth price. Costs vary by procedure, hospital, surgeon, anaesthetist, tests, private-health cover, excess, waiting periods and individual circumstances. Any applicable range or estimate is discussed at consultation, with an itemised breakdown before you decide.
+>
+> **9. Does Medicare cover weight loss surgery?** Medicare benefits may apply when the relevant MBS item, clinical and referral requirements are met, but Medicare does not cover every cost and no rebate should be assumed. The applicable item depends on the procedure—31575 is sleeve gastrectomy, 31572 is Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and 31581 is BPD/duodenal switch—so your surgeon and insurer should confirm what applies.
+>
+> **10. What is the 30/30 eating rule after bariatric surgery?** Many bariatric programs use a 30/30 approach: take about 30 minutes to eat and separate drinks from meals by about 30 minutes. It is a general postoperative guide, not a universal rule; your surgeon or dietitian will tailor advice to your procedure and stage of recovery.
+>
+> **11. What can happen over 10 years after weight loss surgery?** Long-term experiences vary. Some people maintain changes, while others regain weight, develop nutritional issues or need further treatment; ongoing medical, dietary and supplement follow-up may remain important. Your surgeon can discuss the evidence and what your health and follow-up plan may mean for you, but no single 10-year outcome can be promised.
+
+The verified destination slugs available in `content-briefs/` are: `/gastric-sleeve-perth`, `/gastric-bypass-perth`, `/non-surgical-weight-loss`, `/medicare-private-health-cover`, `/weight-loss-surgery-cost-perth`, `/book-consultation`, `/gp-referral`, `/faqs`, `/hospitals-locations` and `/surgeons`.
+
+Use these paste-ready link placements:
